course: dictionary
lesson: 12155
title: Compilation: many things put together
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A compilation is a collection of things put together in one album, book or list. The things might be songs, videos, facts or stories. «Now That's What I Call Music» is a compilation album, because it gathers lots of different songs onto one album.
explain: Compilation can also mean the act of collecting and arranging things. «The compilation of the dictionary took years.» Here the word means the whole job of gathering and putting the words in order, not one single object.
explain: Use context clues. If the sentence talks about clips, songs, facts or poems being gathered together, compilation probably means a collection. Test it: does «a collection of funny animal clips» make sense in place of «a compilation of funny animal clips»? Yes, so your meaning fits.
fact: A compilation is a collection of things put together in one album, book or list.
fact: A compilation album gathers songs from different places or times onto one album.
fact: «A compilation of funny animal clips» means many short videos put together in one video.
fact: Compilation can also mean the act of collecting and arranging things, as in «The compilation of the dictionary took years».
fact: In computing, a compiler turns code written by people into code the computer can run, and this process is called compilation.
exercise: «We made a compilation of our favourite poems for the school show.» What is a compilation here? | A painting of the school | A single poem read out loud | A race to finish first | *A collection of poems put together in one book
exercise: «The compilation of the dictionary took years.» What does compilation mean in this sentence? | A prize for the best speller | A short story about a dog | A dictionary that is missing pages | *The job of collecting and arranging the words
exercise: Which phrase names a collection of funny clips put together in one video? | a loud compilation | a wet compilation | *a compilation video | a sunny compilation
test: Maya's class made a compilation of facts about owls, put into one book. What is the book? | A book about cars | *A collection of owl facts put together | A story with no words | A list of spelling mistakes
test: In computing, what does a compiler turn into code the computer can run? | Pictures into songs | Pages into books | *Code written by people | Computers into people
exam: Which sentence uses compilation correctly? | «The compilation was very hungry.» | «The compilation barked loudly at the postman.» | *«The compilation album has twenty of the band's best songs.» | «She compilation her lunch quickly.»
